{
  "id": "semantic_tokens/preprocessor/09_condition_operands",
  "topic": "semantic_tokens",
  "subtopic": "preprocessor",
  "title": "Macro names in conditions",
  "summary": "A name a condition tests is a `macro`, defined or not",
  "prose": "`#ifdef`, `#ifndef`, `defined(…)`, `#undef` and the names an `#if` tests\nname macros whether or not one is defined; `defined` and checks such as\n`__has_include` are operators, what such a check tests is no macro, and the\nfile `__has_include` tests is a header name.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "#define FEATURE 1\n\n#ifdef FEATURE\nint with_feature = 1;\n#endif\n\n#ifndef MISSING\nint without_missing = 2;\n#endif\n\n#if defined(FEATURE) && !defined(MISSING) && __has_include(\"main.cpp\")\nint all_three = 3;\n#endif\n\n#undef FEATURE\n\n#if __has_include(<missing_header.h>)\nint with_missing_header = 4;\n#endif\n\n#if UNDEFINED_FEATURE || __has_cpp_attribute(nodiscard)\nint with_undefined = 5;\n#endif\n",
      "markers": []
    }
  ],
